\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Motivation of PAMA-SDD++. SDD exposes local classification evidence by partitioning features into regular grids, but a grid cell can contain incomplete object parts, background-biased regions, or uncertain teacher predictions. PAMA-SDD++ filters local targets by reliability and mediates them through pyramid-agent global semantics. }}{1}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:motivation}{{1}{1}{Motivation of PAMA-SDD++. SDD exposes local classification evidence by partitioning features into regular grids, but a grid cell can contain incomplete object parts, background-biased regions, or uncertain teacher predictions. PAMA-SDD++ filters local targets by reliability and mediates them through pyramid-agent global semantics}{figure.1}{}}
